AB  - Ectomycorrhizal (ECM) fungi serve key functions in forest ecosystems by supplying water and nutrients to tree hosts, yet mutualistic plant- fungi interactions are jeopardised by environmental alterations. Here, we discuss the great potential and current limitations of landscape ge-nomics in investigating signatures of local adaptation in natural popu-lations of ECM fungi.
